  "notes": [
    "Import: upstream Lean v4.36.0 (611c117bfa) with Mathlib v4.36.0 (fc4f59e577) and the Batteries it pins (b4b25a3886); the line's patches through 0048 (kernel e4ef4939d6, Emscripten 7.0.0). The import's own changes: src/Lean/Shell.lean (`private` dropped under v4.36's redundantVisibility lint with --wfail; codeQualityEntryTasks reset), v4.36.0's checker pins (nanoda, con-leche, con-ron), and stage0 taken whole from the tag (the two pointer-width gates the line re-applied there changed only a native 32-bit build).",
    "Never mix releases: v4.36 changes persisted layouts (EnvironmentHeader.moduleNames, extension generations, synthCache, IR DeclInfo.maxVar/maxJp, which the interpreter reads without a bound check; CHECK_OLEAN_VERSION is off). Every pack is rebuilt and every snapshot must be rebaked against this runtime's build id; a host must not load an earlier release's packs or snapshots with this runtime, or this release's with an earlier runtime.",
    "0045 (architecture review R11a): dead runtime code removed. The export _lean_wasm_reset is gone (no host called it). _lean_wasm_load_snapshot_mem keeps its three i64 parameters but ignores flags: every load runs the [init] replay; keep passing 1n, which earlier runtimes need. QED64_ALLOW_LEGACY_IMPORTS has no reader (the wasm target tolerates legacy imports as before; native64 keeps stock's guard), so QED64's bake-snapshot --allow-legacy-imports and snapshot-probe --init-flags do nothing. Gone from stderr: [WASM PROFILE] init replay SKIPPED, 12 [WASM DEBUG] lines (0037's waiting on the tasks … line among them) and the [DEBUG:ASSERT] console lines; EMBED-RUNTIME §5's lines and the two [WASM DEBUG] … failed: <error> lines are unchanged.",
    "0046 (architecture review K3): a refused header's one error reads modules #[…] are not loaded in this session, without the ending — use \"Load exact imports\"; match the substring are not loaded in this session. $/qed64/headerStatus.version, and $/lean/ileanHeaderSetupInfo's version, is the version of the document whose header setup the notification reports (it was always the first); a body edit still sends no status, so it can be older than the document's. No protocol change.",
    "0047 (architecture review D3b): 0038's unused knobs and counters are gone: the exports _lean_wasm_task_manager_stat, _lean_wasm_engine_probes and _lean_wasm_engine_guard_trips (the JavaScript contract is 25 names); Module.pthreadPoolSize (the pool is 24 Workers again, -sPTHREAD_POOL_SIZE=24); LEAN_WASM_STD_SURPLUS_EXIT and LEAN_WASM_PARKED_IDLE_MS (no effect). Kept: LEAN_WASM_PARKED_DEDICATED (default 0), _lean_wasm_task_manager_parked_threads, _lean_init_task_manager_using, the 24-Worker pool.",
    "0048: the toolchain moves to Emscripten 7.0.0 (qed64-toolchain:emsdk-7.0.0 on emscripten/emsdk:7.0.0; the native toolchain is unchanged: gcc 13.3.0, glibc 2.39, CMake 3.28.3, Python 3.12.3; the image base moved from Ubuntu 24.04.4 to 24.04.5). For hosts: FS.filesystems is gone: mount Module.NODEFS and Module.WORKERFS (a host that also serves 6.0.5 runtimes reads Module.X ?? FS.filesystems.X); getValue, setValue, ccall and stringToNewUTF8 exist on Module only, and of the exports only _malloc, _pthread_self, __emscripten_proxy_main and __emscripten_check_mailbox keep a global (read _free, _main and every _lean_* on Module); proxiedFunctionTable is sorted ([exitOnMainThread, _proc_exit, …]): find the exit entries by identity (QED64's worker since 58e1918; lean4game re-pins before it runs on this runtime); the glue's #27501 waiter clear is skipped while waitAsyncPolyfilled is true (QED64 sets it in every pthread realm from its HARDENING #94). Allocations and compactor reserves of 4 GiB and more work (0043's 6.0.5 limits, emscripten#28035). Unchanged: a failed C++ new aborts, 0020's keepalive patch is still needed, the proxying lost wakeup #28186 (fixed in 7.0.1) remains, an imported memory's heap stops 0-128 MiB short of its maximum.",
    "Tools 4.36.0-e4ef493: a lean4-wasm64 gate from 4.35.0-0bf1fb2 or earlier fails this runtime, in S2 (_lean_wasm_reset and 0038's three counters; its [0038] checks skip) and, on 7.0.0, in S6 and at its node-runner's FS.filesystems: gate it with this release's tools (QED64: adopt-release --tools), which still pass the published 6.0.5 runtimes. The gate: S6 in two lines (K6, the glue names QED64's worker reads; the rest) and a note for what only lean4game's pinned worker reads; new checks for the glue's 24-Worker pool and [default: no parking]; the ten [0038] checks are gone. node-runner and persistent-probe take NODEFS from Module or FS.filesystems; LEAN4_WASM64_PTHREAD_POOL and LEAN4_WASM64_RTSTATS are gone; runtime-knobs.mjs drops poolModuleKeys, runtimeStats and TASK_MANAGER_STATS and adds glueFilesystem and vfsExists. exports-audit fails on BARE reads of Module-only names and marks the PThread/TTY/FS members a given glue lacks. stage-release refuses a by-value runtime whose recipe's FROM is not its BASE_IMG; native64.sh and mathlib-tree.sh refuse a build dir of another recipe.",
    "Packs: mathlib-essential's roots gain Mathlib.Tactic.Cases, Mathlib.Tactic.Have, Mathlib.Tactic.NormNum.Prime, Mathlib.Combinatorics.Pigeonhole and Mathlib.Topology.Instances.Real.Lemmas (architecture review D12 b-lite; js/packs.json holds the one list). mathlib-game-extra's roots are lean4game's generated list (wasm/mathlib-roots.txt at lean4game 7761013, copied byte for byte: the 91 modules the catalog games, GameServer and lean-i18n import directly; checked at Mathlib v4.36.0 and Batteries b4b25a3886). It names Mathlib.Algebra.Order.Star.{Int,Rat} (Mathlib.Data.{Int,Rat}.Star stay as Mathlib's deprecated_module shims) and Batteries.Tactic.OpenPrivate. mathlib-essential: 4,526 modules, 98 of them deprecated_module shims (v4.35: 4,438); mathlib-game-extra: 746, 6 shims (v4.35: 721). Leave every pack while they still exist upstream: Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Log.Base and Mathlib.Data.Int.Log (no game or proof sheet imports them), Mathlib.MeasureTheory.Measure.Typeclasses.NoAtoms (a deprecated_module shim at v4.35, a real module outside every closure at v4.36). Move from mathlib-essential to mathlib-game-extra: Mathlib.Tactic.Linter.AuxLemma, Mathlib.Tactic.Linter.OldObtain. Deleted upstream, so gone with no shim: 7 core modules (Lean.Meta.Tactic.Grind.Arith.{CommRing.Functions, CommRing.MonadRing, CommRing.MonadSemiring, EvalNum, Insts}, Lean.Meta.Tactic.Grind.OrderInsts, Std.Internal.Order.PropLattice) and 5 Mathlib ones (Mathlib.Algebra.Field.Power, Mathlib.Data.NNRat.Order, Mathlib.Order.Bounded, Mathlib.Tactic.Inclusion.Extension.Interval, Mathlib.Tactic.Linter.UnusedTacticExtension).",
    "Known limits: `bv_decide (config := { uf := true })` reaches the runtime's in-process CaDiCaL stub, which panics and ends the whole wasm runtime (opt-in; the default is false). `idbg` in a do block aborts at the TCP stub (as before).",
    "Stack, measured against lean-v4.35.0-0bf1fb2 (Node v26.3.0 CLI, the builds interleaved, two sessions): on deep elaboration recursion (a Fin 40 x Fin 40 `decide`) this runtime needs about 18 KiB (2-3%) more pthread stack. The smallest LEAN4_WASM64_PTHREAD_STACK_MB that completes it moves from 0.877 to 0.895 MiB with the 0036 guard off (the engine's peak; the second session agreed within one bisection step) and from about 0.99 to 1.009 MiB with it on. Most of it comes from Lean v4.36, a few KiB from Emscripten 7; the kernel probe (`decide +kernel`) is unchanged. At Chrome's worker stack (about 0.68 MiB) both runtimes stop that probe at the guard with the thread alive, so code near the limit can reach the guard a little earlier. No speed regression was measured.",
    "native64: built from e4ef4939d6 in qed64-toolchain:emsdk-7.0.0 (its native toolchain unchanged); v4.36 builds CaDiCaL from source and ships lib/lean/libcadical.a and libinitialize_minimal_shim.a.",
    "Gate: gate-dir 83/0, with QED64's resident probe 93/0, full gate (--mathlib-lib, --resident-probe) 107/0 (0bf1fb2: 90 and full 114; the ten [0038] checks are gone, three are new). Build id wasm64-24f92aa50d027c97."
  ],
